## Test A, averaging (pre-declared): at each ratio, (a) backlog CV over slots falls from m50 to m200 (Mann-Whitney, one-sided) and (b) the v5 + MDD-TECT ceiling still shrinks from m50 to m200 (per-instance %, Mann-Whitney, one-sided: m200 less negative). Supported if (a) and (b) hold at r 0.80.
- r0.35: backlog CV m50 0.60 -> m200 0.47 (p 0.00256); v5+TECT ceiling per instance m50 -11.51% -> m200 -20.49% median (p 0.993)
- r0.52: backlog CV m50 0.53 -> m200 0.51 (p 0.318); v5+TECT ceiling per instance m50 -19.50% -> m200 -19.21% median (p 0.484)
- r0.80: backlog CV m50 0.55 -> m200 0.48 (p 0.0169); v5+TECT ceiling per instance m50 -19.55% -> m200 -11.00% median (p 0.0234)
  -> averaging SUPPORTED at r 0.80 (a True, b True)

## Test B, transport scarcity (pre-declared): on m100 and m200, (c) the v5 ceiling at r 0.80 is larger than at r 0.52 (same instances, per-instance %, Wilcoxon) and (d) what MDD-TECT adds over the v5 oracle is larger at r 0.35 than at r 0.80 (paired, Wilcoxon). Supported if (c) and (d) hold on both floors.
- m100 (n 20): v5 ceiling per instance, median r0.35 / 0.52 / 0.80: -1.36 / -4.93 / -10.84%; (c) r0.80 - r0.52 median -2.12 pts, p 0.0483 -> True. MDD-TECT adds, median r0.35 / 0.52 / 0.80: -11.85 / -1.29 / -0.04%; (d) r0.35 - r0.80 median -11.24 pts, p 5.34e-05 -> True
- m200 (n 20): v5 ceiling per instance, median r0.35 / 0.52 / 0.80: -0.97 / -1.14 / -2.61%; (c) r0.80 - r0.52 median -1.28 pts, p 0.00639 -> True. MDD-TECT adds, median r0.35 / 0.52 / 0.80: -20.24 / -18.66 / -6.26%; (d) r0.35 - r0.80 median -14.40 pts, p 0.0121 -> True
  -> transport scarcity SUPPORTED (m100 True, m200 True)

